# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Derived data -- excluded because it is regenerable and large.
#
# The rule: commit what cannot be recreated (the raw recordings), plus the
# extracted pool and the results. Everything reconstructible from those by
# running a command stays out, because binary audio does not delta-compress,
# so every committed byte stays in history forever.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 165 MB/session of 48 kHz WAV, rebuilt in seconds from unconverted_raw/:
#     ./convert_recordings.ps1 -Session day_N
converted_wavs/

# ~11 MB, rebuilt from training_clips/ in about a minute:
#     python features.py --out day_N/dataset.npz
# build_dataset is deterministic (sorted globs, deterministic mel), so a rebuild
# is byte-identical and evaluate.py's dataset-hash guard still matches the
# committed checkpoints.
# By NAME, not *.npz -- dataset_pilot.npz is kept: its source clips no longer
# exist, so it cannot be regenerated.
dataset.npz

# build/ is the scratch area: smoke checkpoints, throwaway datasets, plots made
# while iterating. Everything in it is ignored, but the directory itself is kept
# so it survives a clone and tools can write there without mkdir.
build/*
!build/.gitkeep

# Stray scratch outputs at the repo ROOT. The leading slash matters:
# per-session checkpoints in day_N/ ARE committed -- they are results.
/ckpt_*.pt
/checkpoint.pt
/checkpoint_coatnet.pt
/confusion.png

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/

# Per-machine Claude Code permissions (hardcodes this box's Python path).
# .claude/settings.json, if one is ever added, IS shared and stays tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Project instructions for Claude Code, kept local -- it has personal/career
# planning content not meant for the public repo. Still auto-loaded from the
# repo root when working here; it just isn't tracked.
/CLAUDE.md

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
